==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[ˈsiː.zn̩]||a=RP}}

* {{IPA|en|[ˈsi.zn̩]||a=GA}}, {{enPR|sēʹzən}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-season.ogg|a=US}}

* {{IPA|en|[ˈsɪi.zən]||a=AU}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-season.ogg|a=AU}}

* {{rhymes|en|iːzən|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|sea|son}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*seh₁-|id=sow}}
From {{inh|en|enm|sesoun|sesoun, seson|time of the year}}, from {{der|en|fro|seson|seson, saison|time of sowing, seeding}}, from {{der|en|la|satiō||act of sowing, planting}} from {{m|la|satum}}, past participle of {{m|la|serō||to sow, plant}} from {{der|en|ine-pro|*seh₁-||to sow, plant}}. Akin to {{cog|ang|sāwan||to sow}}, {{m|ang|sǣd||seed}}. {{doublet|en|saison}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|sele||season}} (from {{cog|ang|sǣl||season, time, occasion}}), {{cog|enm|tide||season, time of year}} (from {{cog|ang|tīd||time, period, yeartide, season}}).

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q24384}} Each of the divisions of a [[year]] based on the prevailing weather: [[spring]], [[summer]], [[autumn]] ([[fall]]) and [[winter]]; or the [[rainy season|rainy]] ([[monsoon season|monsoon]]) and [[dry season]], depending on the climate.
#: {{syn|en|yeartide|yeartime}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=c. 1705|author=w:Joseph Addison|title=Remarks on several parts of Italy, &c. in the years 1701, 1702, 1703
|passage=we saw, in six days' traveling, the several '''seasons''' of the year in their beauty and perfection}}
#* {{quote-song |en |lyricist={{w|Jaques Brel}} (original version); w:Rod McKuen |title=Seasons in the Sun |artist=w:Terry Jacks |year=1973 |passage=We had joy, we had fun, we had '''seasons''' in the sun, / But the wine and the song, / like the '''seasons''', have all gone.}}
# A period of the year when something particular happens.
#: {{syn|en|time}}
#: {{ux|en|mating '''season'''}}
#: {{ux|en|the football '''season'''}}
#: {{ux|en|the holiday '''season'''}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand. We spent consider'ble money getting 'em reset, and then a swordfish got into the pound and tore the nets all to slathers, right in the middle of the squiteague '''season'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:National Geographic|year=1987|month=October|volume=172|number=4|title=North Carolina's Outer Banks|author=Charles E. Cobb, Jr.|page=507
|text=Since a state ban was lifted in 1984, hunters may shoot one swan per '''season'''. A permit system limited last '''season's''' take to 6,000.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Matias Grez|title=Steph Curry accepts assistant general manager role at alma mater Davidson College|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/03/11/sport/steph-curry-assistant-gm-davidson-college-spt-intl|date=2025-03-11|passage=Curry, a four-time NBA champion with the Warriors, played for the Wildcats for three '''seasons''' between 2006 and 2009, where he was twice named conference player of the year. {{...}} Curry has been named NBA regular '''season''' MVP twice and is an 11-time All Star.}}
# A period of the year in which a [[place]] is most busy or frequented for business, amusement, etc.
#* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|passage=He seldom was seen in the office himself, but occasionally a paragraph in the paper recorded that his yacht had touched at Mentone and that he had been seen at the Monte Carlo tables, or that he was expected in Leicestershire for the '''season'''.}}
# {{lb|en|pars pro toto|metonymy}} A year, but with emphasis on the most important part of the year in context, such as the months when plants or animals grow and reproduce.
#: {{ux|en|This invasive species reproduces so rapidly that it can completely take over an area in just a couple '''seasons'''.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} The [[period]] over which a [[series]] of [[Test match]]es are played.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} That which gives [[relish]]; seasoning.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing|4|1|text=O! she is fallen<br>Into a pit of ink, that the wide sea<br>Hath drops too few to wash her clean again,<br>And salt too little which may '''season''' give<br>To her foul-tainted flesh.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|III|4|text=You lack the '''season''' of all natures, sleep.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q3464665}} {{lb|en|North America|Australia|broadcasting}} A group of episodes of a television or radio program broadcast in regular intervals with a long break between each group, usually with one year between the beginning of each.
#: {{syn|en|[[series]]<qq:British English>}}
#: {{ux|en|The third '''season''' of ''Robot Chicken'' aired from 2007 to 2008.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=February 11, 1998|episode=w:Tom's Rhinoplasty|title=w:South Park|season=1|number=11|passage=Or - is she Erin Gray in the second '''season''' of Buck Rogers beautiful?}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} An extended, undefined period of time.
#* {{RQ:Milton Poems|On the Morning of Christs Nativity|2|It was the Winter wilde.<br>While the Heav’n-born-childe,<br>All meanly wrapt in the rude manger lies:<br>Nature in aw to him<br>Had doff't her gawdy trim,<br>With her great Maſter ſo to ſympathize:<br>It was no '''ſeaſon''' then for her<br>To wanton with the Sun her luſty Paramour.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1656|author=[[w:John Owen (theologian)|John Owen]]|title=The Mortification of Sin
|passage=So it is in a person when a breach hath been made upon his conscience, quiet, perhaps credit, by his lust, in some eruption of actual sin; — carefulness, indignation, desire, fear, revenge are all set on work about it and against it, and lust is quiet for a '''season''', being run down before them; but when the hurry is over and the inquest is past, the thief appears again alive, and is as busy as ever at his work.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=John Buchan|title=The Outgoing of the Tide
|passage=A '''season''' of great doubt fell upon her soul.}}
# {{lb|en|[[wikipedia:Evangelical Christianity|Evangelical Christianity]]}} A period of time in one’s life characterized by a particular emotion of situation.
#: {{ux|en|a '''season''' of faithlessness}}
# {{lb|en|video games}} The full set of [[downloadable]] [[content]] for a game, which can be purchased with a [[season pass]].
# {{lb|en|video games}} A fixed period of time in a [[massively multiplayer online game]] in which new content (themes, rules, modes, etc.) becomes available, sometimes replacing earlier content.

=====Usage notes=====
In British English, a year-long group of episodes of a television or radio show is called a {{m|en|series|id=Q3464665}}, whereas in North American English the word {{m|en|series}} is a synonym of {{m|en|program}} or {{m|en|show}}.

