===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|id=cut}}
From {{inh|en|enm|scren}}, {{m|enm|screne||windscreen, firescreen}}, from {{der|en|xno|escren||firescreen, the tester of a bed}}, {{der|en|fro|escren}}, {{m|fro|escrein}}, {{m|fro|escran}} (modern {{cog|fr|écran||screen}}), from {{der|en|dum|scherm}}, from {{der|en|odt|skirm}}, from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*skirmi}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*skirmiz||fur, shelter, covering, screen}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut, divide}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|scherm||screen}}, {{cog|de|Schirm||screen}}. {{doublet|en|scherm}}.

An alternative etymology derives {{cog|fro|escren}}, {{m|fro|escran}} from {{der|en|odt|*scranc|t=barrier}} (compare {{cog|dum|schranc}}, {{m|dum|schranke|t=palisade, trellis, grid}}, {{cog|de|Schrank|t=cupboard, cabinet}}, {{cog|de|Schranke|t=fence}}), from {{der|en|gmw-pro|*skrank}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*skrankaz}}.<ref>''Webster's Encyclopedic Unabridged Dictionary of the English Language'', s.v. "screen" (NY: Gramercy Books, 1996), 1721.</ref>

